  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WATER RESOURCES MANAGEMENT SECTOR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE SECTOR REVIEW WILL EXAMINE A BROAD RANGE OF ISSUES, INCLUDING: (I) AVAILABLE LITERATURE ON WATER RES. &amp; MGT.; (A) WATER QUANTITY  &amp; QUALITY CONSTRAINTS; (B) LEGAL, REGULATORY &amp; INST. FRAMEWORKS FOR WATER RES. MGT.; (C) DROUGHT PREPAREDNESS; (D) CURRENT DELIVERYSYST.  &amp;  PRICING POLICIES FOR WATER; (E) POTENTIAL ROLES FOR PRIVATESECTOR &amp; COM.PARTICIPATION IN WATER RES. MGT.; (F)ENV.  &amp;  SOCIAL ASPECTSOF WATER MGT. &amp; DEV.;(G) INT&apos;NAL WATER ISSUES; (H) CAPACITY BUILDING &amp;(I)FUTURE WATER USE PLANS. THE REVIEW WILL BE CARRIED OUT BY A TEAM OF NAMIBIAN WATER PROFESSIONALS WITH SUPPORT FROM INTERNATIONAL EXPERTS AS NECESSARY.  DRAFT REPORTS WILL BE PRESENTED AT STAKEHOLDER WORKSHOPS, AND THE INPUTS OF THOSE WORKSHOPS INCORPORATED IN FINAL REPORTS AS APPROPRIATE.  THE OUTPUT OF THE TASK WILL BE THEMATIC REPORTS ON SOME 5-7 ISSUE AREAS.</narrative>
  </description>
